  "jobTitle": "Principal Software Engineer-Associate Tek Fellow",
  "summary": "PROFILE\n-Extensive project and design engineering experience.\n-Background includes UML design, expert systems (artificial intelligence), controls, image processing,  systems integration/requirement analysis,  software and hardware microprocessor based design,  and digital circuit design.\n-Worked in Research and Development and brought in contracts for further development of Expert Systems begun using R&D funds.\n-Strong communications, organizational, and problem solving skills.\n-Authored and co-authored publications and presentations.\n-Able to perform well in demanding environments and meet deadlines.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n-Extensive experience (9-years) with G2 real-time expert system \"shell\" and its integration into existing monitoring/control systems (G2 is used for industrial process monitoring/control) \n-Operating Systems:  Windows, SunWorkstation/UNIX, VAX/VMS\n-Languages:  Microsoft Visual C++,  C++,  G2,  C,  Assembly,  FORTRAN,  PASCAL,  ADA,  LISP,  SNOBOL,  Microprogramming,  VHDL,  PV-WAVE,\nincluding system level programming,  device drivers for serial and ethernet ports, client/server architectures,  embedded software, compilers\n-Microprocessors:  software/hardware for Intel 4004, 4040, 8080, 80286, and 8748, RCA 1802, National COPS 420, Motorola 6800, 6801, Zilog 8000\n-Graphics Controller:  Intel 82720\n-Knowledge of TTL, CMOS, and analog ICs\n-Have designed digital circuits (10 years),  fiber optic systems,  concurrent multiprocessor systems,  hardware/software for microprocessors ,  transmitters,  receivers,  control circuits,  filters,  multiplexers,  amplifiers,  D/A and A/D converters,  displays,  memories,  etc.\n\nSpecialties: Diagnostics, Prognostics and Health Mangement, other Expert Systems, G2 knowledge bases and integration software, C++",
