    "description": "PRATT&WHITNEY ROCKETDYNE/BOEING/MCDONNELL DOUGLASS/ROCKWELL Inc., \n-Developed software to automate the use of a Tektronix Logic Analyzer (for data acquisition and analysis) during Verification and Validation (V&V) tests for the Space Shuttle Main Engine (SSME) Controller Software.\n-Developed software to integrate the Tektronix Logic Analyzer Automation Software into the SSME Controller Software and Hardware in the Loop Laboratory System Software.\n-Developed Software Requirements and presentations for the J-2X. \n-Developed software requirement specifications for the Linear Engine Model for the SSME Advanced Health Management System.  \n-Developed automated test procedures for the airborne transmitter receiver system for Connexion by Boeing.\n-Developed interface software to provide G2 systems with telemetry/server/simulator data, and provide archiving/playback capabilities for the US Space Lab Subsystems.\n-Developed DoD application software for a wearable computer.\n-Developed engine plume image processing software to detect SSME anomalies\n-Leading a team of engineers in developing an Expert System for real-time SSME Test monitoring/problem detecting/problem solving/control.\n-Lead a team of engineers to develop detailed operating requirements for a Microcircuit Obsolescence Solutions Expert System for the Army Industrial Operations.\n-Served in an advising capacity to develop a Launch Countdown Monitoring/Problem Detecting/Problem Advisory Expert System for the ATLAS.\n-Developed software for the Solid Rocket Booster Thrust Vector Control System to evaluate static firing data. Computed nozzle positions, nozzle pivot point migration, and evaluated instrumentation.\n-Evaluated and developed chart presentations of SRB reentry trajectory and environment.\n-Developed an RLC model of the Space Shuttle Main Engine.\n-Performed requirement analysis of Ground Support Equipment and Cryogenics Loading Software for Vandenberg Air Force Base and Kennedy Space Center.",
